& [ImplementationProofCoverage] is the accepted behavior coverage for IR3 operator harness implementation
  + [covered_behavior] is operator requests parse into validated contract-bound request records without throwing for malformed fixture input
  + [covered_behavior] is stale authority produces blocked_output with stale_refusal and no operator_result
  + [covered_behavior] is missing contract version produces blocked_output with missing_contract_version
  + [covered_behavior] is undeclared output produces fault_output with operator_contract_violation
  + [covered_behavior] is generated projection presented as authority produces fault_output with generated_trace_authority_confusion
  + [covered_behavior] is ambiguous input identity produces sop_first_interrupt with ambiguous_identity
  + [covered_behavior] is unsupported scope produces blocked_output with unsupported_scope
  + [covered_behavior] is unsafe operations requests produce fault_output with unsupported_operations_control and no live dispatch output
  + [covered_behavior] is deterministic replay mismatch is represented as a fixture-level fault proof
  + [covered_behavior] is generated output path escape and source mutation attempts are refused before writes
  + [covered_behavior] is generated output write is accepted only under ignored generated roots
  + [covered_behavior] is authority discovery excludes tests/fixtures/generated/ir3_operator_harness paths
  + [covered_behavior] is generated test outputs are cleaned after tests and remain reproducible

  = must: require a future slice before widening fixture cases, output paths, dependency set, or authority semantics

& [DownstreamIR4GateExport] is the downstream gate exported by this proof pack
  + [IR4_state] is may_open_only_after_IR3_implementation_completion_review_accepts_this_pack
  + [IR4_entry_model_route] is requires deeper reasoning for downstream boundary and authority/projection handoff
  + [future_spark_suitable_work] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable only after IR4 slices define bounded implementation work
  + [safety_limit] is no live operations control authorized

  = must: open IR4 by minting or accepting a downstream boundary, not by directly adding LangGraph runtime, surface adapter, queue, operations simulator, operations control, or live machine control
  = must: preserve IR3 operator harness proof as boundary input for future coordination/runtime work

& [IR3ImplementationProofPackInvalidationRuleSet] is the staleness contract for IR3OperatorHarnessImplementationProofPackV1
  + [invalidated_by] is change to any accepted implementation output hash
  + [invalidated_by] is change to any accepted fixture source or expected-ledger hash
  + [invalidated_by] is change to generated-output proof or contract tests
  + [invalidated_by] is change to IR3-IA01 through IR3-IA06 completion or repair reviews that affects support, requirements, or gates
  + [invalidated_by] is generated projection promoted to source authority
  + [invalidated_by] is source fixture, expected ledger, source code, platform authority, or docs authority mutated by runtime code or tests
  + [invalidated_by] is dependency installation without authorizing slice
  + [invalidated_by] is operations control or live machine control leak

  = must: rerun IR3-IA07 or rebake the relevant surface after invalidation before downstream work consumes this proof pack
